    <md:title>5.7.1: Patterns in Real Numbers</md:title>
    <md:uuid>92179e8d-61dc-4083-bb44-83e450eff137</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
<para>In the table, find as many patterns as you can. Use one or more patterns to help you complete the table. Be prepared to explain your reasoning.</para>
<table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
  <thead>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis"> fraction </entry>
      <entry> \(\frac12\) </entry>
      <entry> \(\frac14\) </entry>
      <entry> \(\frac18\) </entry>
      <entry> \(\frac{1}{16}\) </entry>
      <entry> \(\frac{1}{32}\) </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">decimal</entry>
      <entry> 0.5 </entry>
      <entry> 0.25 </entry>
      <entry> 0.125 </entry>
      <entry> a._____ </entry>
      <entry> b._____ </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>
<!--Interaction End -->
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="c77542e5-a428-463d-916d-0f3cc8b0af5e" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="0" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <exercise data-content-id="cb38133c-fc76-4a75-bb30-617cc34e630d" data-problem-comparator="float" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="0.0625">
    <problem>
      <para> What is the value for a? </para>
      <para> Enter your answer here: </para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para> Correct! 0.0625</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <exercise data-content-id="5873a187-8e12-472a-bba2-e3dc88a7f04d" data-problem-comparator="float" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="0.03125">
    <problem>
      <para> What is the value for b? </para>
      <para> Enter your answer here: </para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para> Correct! 0.03125</para>
    </solution>
        </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below this line-->
  <solution> </solution>
  </div>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para> Describe the pattern you used to find the values that completed the table.</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answers:</para>
    <list>
      <item> Each number is half of the previous number. We can find the next number by multiplying the current number by \(\frac12\) or by 0.5, or by dividing by 2. </item>
      <item> The non-zero digits of the decimals are powers of 5 (\(5^1\), \(5^2\), \(5^3\), etc.), and each time there is an additional decimal place. </item>
      <item> 0.5 can be written as \(\frac{5}{10}\), 0.25 as \(\frac{25}{100}\), and 0.125 as \(\frac{125}{1,000}\). The numerators are powers of 5, and the denominators are powers of 10, so the next two numbers are \(\frac{5^4}{10^4}\), which is \(\frac{65}{10,000}\) or 0.0625, and \(\frac{5^5}{10^5}\), which is \(\frac{3,125}{100,000}\) or 0.03125. </item>
      <item> The denominators in the fractions are powers of 2. </item>
    </list>
  </solution></exercise></section>
